    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>By observing the data given, by doubling the pressure, half-life is reduced to half. This result is following second order kinetics. Mathematically it can be proved as follows,</p><p>The half-life and initial pressure of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi>th</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;order reaction can be related as follows,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub><mo>&#8733;</mo><msup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msub></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></msub></mfenced><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mfenced><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>50</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Hence, the order of the reaction is second order.</p>"
  }
